withdraw decrements amount and writes the entry back. When the balance reaches zero the entry stays in persistent storage forever: still occupying a ledger entry, still accruing rent, still needing TTL extension by Sorokeep''s guard. For a project whose stated purpose is showcasing storage lifecycle management, accumulating dead entries is the wrong default. Decide before implementing, because deleting has its own consequence — the vault id is consumed and a later get_vault returns VaultNotFound rather than a zero balance.

